# Evidence store — encrypted customer data, never committed
data/

# Real-corpus script state (Story 4.2): Cipher lookup cache + API call budget,
# and the duplicate-run lock file — local, generated, never committed.
# Scoped to calibration_model_v1.json's own lock file specifically, not a
# bare *.lock -- that would also silently ignore unrelated legitimate lock
# files (e.g. poetry.lock, yarn.lock) if this repo ever adds one (code
# review 2026-08-03). Every lock file this codebase's acquire_run_lock
# creates is named f"{resource_path}.lock", and the only resource_path in
# practice is calibration_model_v1.json (both fit_real_calibration_model.py
# and run_evaluation_harness.py lock on it).
.sentinel_script_state.db
calibration_model_v1.json.lock

# run_evaluation_harness.py's per-file results (Story 4.1 follow-up,
# 2026-08-05): local, generated real-run output, never committed -- unlike
# calibration_model_v1.json itself (the actual product artifact), this is
# a diagnostic record of one specific run, not something to ship.
# Anchored to the repo root (where _RESULTS_PATH actually writes) -- a bare
# `results.json` would also match the unrelated, already-tracked
# eval/results.json, the exact class of overbroad pattern the
# calibration_model_v1.json.lock comment above already warns against
# (code review 2026-08-05).
/results.json

